@startuml
title Smart Shopping - Proposed Kubernetes Deployment (design, not a running cluster)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam node {
  BorderColor #B52330
  BackgroundColor #FFF4F4
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #202025
  BackgroundColor #EEEEEE
}
skinparam cloud {
  BorderColor #777777
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FAF5F5
skinparam LegendBorderColor #B52330
top to bottom direction

node "Shopper / Operator Browser" as Browser #FFFFFF

cloud "CI/CD\nGitHub Actions + container registry\nGitOps controller" as CICD
cloud "External LLM Provider\n(large model, European provider preferred)" as LLM
cloud "Approved price source\n(CSV or API)" as Src
cloud "Electricity Maps API (optional, live)" as EMaps

node "Kubernetes cluster - namespace smart-shopping" {
  node "Ingress + TLS" as Ingress
  node "Pool standard (fast, default)" as PS {
    node "Frontend Deployment\n(Shopper Client, Operator Console)\n2 proposed replicas" as FE
    node "Backend Deployment\nShopping API, Assistant Service,\nLLM Gateway, Policy admin, Watch Monitor\n2-3 proposed replicas (HPA)" as API
    database "PostgreSQL 16\nStatefulSet + PVC (demo)" as DB
    node "Kafka (KRaft, 1 broker)\ntopics price.changed, mode.changed,\nevents.dead" as EB
    node "Prometheus + Grafana\n+ OpenTelemetry collector" as Mon
  }
  node "Controllers (CronJobs and one Deployment)" as CTL {
    node "carbon-controller CronJob, every 5 min\nCarbon Monitor + Policy Engine evaluation" as CC
    node "forecast-scheduler CronJob, every 15 min\nJob Scheduler (starts weekly evaluation Job)" as FSch
    node "watch-check CronJob, every 30 min\nWatch Monitor (price watch alerts)" as WChk
    node "price-import CronJob, daily\nPrice Importer (concurrencyPolicy Forbid)" as Imp
    node "placement-controller Deployment (Helm chart)\nPlacement Controller" as PCd
  }
  node "Flexible workloads (steered by taints)" as FLEX {
    node "Forecast Worker and Model Evaluation Jobs\nparallelism set by operating mode" as FWJ
    node "Local Model Runtime Deployment\n(small open-weight model)" as LMRd
  }
  node "Pool eco (simulated low-carbon / low-price node group)" as PE
  node "Energy Signal Simulator Deployment\nintensity, price, renewable flag,\nPrometheus metrics" as SIM
  node "Kepler DaemonSet (pod energy metrics)" as Kep
  node "ConfigMap (policy defaults)\nSecrets (credentials)" as Cfg
}

Browser --> Ingress : HTTPS
Ingress --> FE
Ingress --> API : /api
API --> DB : SQL
API --> LMRd : small model
API --> LLM : large model
CC --> SIM : read signals
CC ..> EMaps : optional
CC --> DB : samples, mode
FSch --> FWJ : create Jobs
FWJ --> DB : forecasts, logs
Imp --> Src : fetch batches
Imp --> DB : upsert
WChk --> DB : alerts
CTL --> EB : publish and\nsubscribe events
EB --> API : mode.changed
PCd --> FLEX : taints\n(evict, reschedule)
FLEX ..> PE : AMBER, RED,\nrenewable
CTL ..> Mon
API ..> Mon
FLEX ..> Mon
Kep ..> Mon
CICD --> API : image tags in Git,\nsynchronised

legend bottom
  Operating mode and policy live in the database and are read by every workload (no redeploy to change them);
  the events only tell consumers earlier. The Placement Controller changes taints so flexible workloads move between pools
  (standard pool in GREEN, eco pool in AMBER, RED or when renewable energy is available).
  Topics: price.changed (Price Importer to Job Scheduler), mode.changed (Policy Engine to Job Scheduler, Gateway, Placement Controller).
  ConfigMap (policy defaults) and Secrets (credentials) are mounted by the backend and the controllers.
  The CronJobs only start work; carbon policy, deadlines and idempotency are enforced by persisted state.
  concurrencyPolicy Forbid avoids overlapping runs but does not guarantee exactly-once execution.
endlegend
@enduml
